Note: Thirty-five of the attempted suicide cases were considered to be manipulative gestures on the part of the inmates concerned. However, there is no positive way to differentiate between those and genuine suicidal attempts.

1. The 9
persons to be appointed by the Governor in Council as members of the National Library Advisory Board under Section 9(2)(d) of the National Library Act have not been appointed as yet by the Governor in Council; the 2 persons provided under (c) have been nominated by the Canada Council and the Association of Universities and Colleges of Canada and their names will be released when all appointments are completed.
2.	The present members of Council are the ex officio members, that is Dr. J. G. Sylvestre, National Librarian; Mr. Erik J. Spicer, Parliamentary Librarian; Dr. W. I. Smith, Dominion Archivist and Dr. Jack E. Brown, Librarian of the National Science Library of the National Research Council of Canada.
